[REQUIREMENT]
MID: feb4cb915f91d319078204293f6cf99eb50e775a8f670e478e30e84bd6979a14
HASH: 17745d554ee1aca155176037541afce34a4c901070a0bdc84d114e8a147a8052
SPDX-Req-Sys: Character Drivers and Misc
TITLE: memory_lseek
COMMENT: >>>
The memory devices use the full 32/64 bits of the offset, and so we cannot
check against negative addresses: they are ok. The return value is weird,
though, in that case (0).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Also note that seeking relative to the "end of file" isn't supported:
it has no meaning, so passing orig equal to SEEK_END returns -EINVAL.
<<<

